#
# Declarative competency question for the kernel slice, authored as slice-resident
# test-DSL data and executed by the native Rust slice-test harness
# (crates/slicetest). One fully-enumerated SELECT — "what aboutness modes
# can a carrier bear toward its subject?" — the slice-resident twin of
# test_competency_aboutness_modes_query in tests/test_aboutness.py. Runs in the
# default asserted lane (gmeow:reasoningNone): the two seeds are directly typed,
# so the expected rows were MEASURED over the asserted graph. See docs/TESTING.md.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/kernel/tests/> .

# queries/competency/aboutness-modes.rq projects ?mode a gmeow:AboutnessMode.
# The complete answer is exactly the two mention/use seeds, so cqExactRows true.
ex:cqAboutnessModes a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "queries/competency/aboutness-modes.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "GMEOW must be able to answer 'what aboutness modes can an information carrier bear toward its subject?'. The asserted answer is the complete, closed two-member value vocabulary of the mention/use axis: gmeow:aboutnessDescribes and gmeow:aboutnessEnacts, with no privileged winner (Principle 9)." ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow
        ex:cqAboutnessRowDescribes ,
        ex:cqAboutnessRowEnacts .

ex:cqAboutnessRowDescribes a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ;
        gmeow:cellVar "mode" ;
        gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:aboutnessDescribes ] .

ex:cqAboutnessRowEnacts a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ;
        gmeow:cellVar "mode" ;
        gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:aboutnessEnacts ] .
